Converting decimal number to binary

¢ We can convert decimal number to binary and
binary to decimal.

¢ From decimal to binary,
— we use either sum of weight method or

— divide the whole number side by 2, keeping the
remainders till we get a zero. The answer is written
in ascending order

¢ For decimals, we multiply the fractional bits by 2
keeping the overflow. The answer is then written
in descending order



Sum of Weight

¢ Here we break the decimal number into the
weight of binary equivalent and add them
together replacing missing weights with zero

